---
source: crates/binsight/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_of(&[\"admin\", \"--help\"]).await"
---
Inspect and maintain an installation

Usage: binsight admin [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  config           Show the effective configuration and where each value comes from (secrets are hidden)
  backup           Back up the database now (works while the server runs)
  db-status        Show the database schema version, pending migrations and projections
  rotate-sessions  Sign out every session by replacing the session secret (the server must be stopped)
  wallet-add       Track a wallet; its history is imported when the server starts (the server must be stopped)
  sync-status      Show how far each wallet is imported and the credits spent (works while the server runs)
  export-tx        Print a stored transaction exactly as the RPC node returned it (works while the server runs)
  repair           Plan a full repair of a wallet's listing and print its credit cost; --apply asks for it (the server must be stopped; it runs when the server starts)
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --config-file <PATH>  The configuration file to read [default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/binsight/binsight.env or ~/.config/binsight/binsight.env]
  -h, --help                Print help
  -V, --version             Print version
